# Known-unfixed bare-name `git fetch` sites, for scripts/preflight/fetch-hygiene.sh.
#
# Format: <path><TAB><normalized command>
#
# This is a SHRINKING list, not an allowlist to add to. Every entry is a bug:
# the fetch resolves a refname git has to disambiguate, and this repo publishes
# `refs/tags/dev`, so `git fetch origin dev` would fetch the TAG and leave
# origin/dev stale (#956, #1158). Add no new entries -- fix the site.
#
# The four below are #1158's workflow half. They cannot be fixed from a lane
# here: the coding agent's installation token has no `workflows` permission, so
# any push touching .github/workflows/** is refused. Delete an entry in the same
# PR that replaces the line with
#   git fetch --no-tags --prune origin \
#     "+refs/heads/<branch>:refs/remotes/origin/<branch>"
# (the guard fails on a stale entry, which is what keeps this list honest).
# When all four are gone, delete this file and the guard's `--baseline` default
# keeps working with an empty list.
.github/workflows/cli.yml	git fetch --no-tags origin "${GITHUB_BASE_REF}" 2>/dev/null || true
.github/workflows/publish-gh-pages-raw.yml	git fetch origin gh-pages
.github/workflows/server.yml	git fetch --no-tags origin "${GITHUB_BASE_REF}" 2>/dev/null || true
.github/workflows/server.yml	git fetch --no-tags origin "${GITHUB_BASE_REF}"
